WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.360
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:10.140
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:17.121
Unit three: Skimming and Scanning. Today you will read academic texts quickly for the main idea or a detail.

4
00:00:17.421 --> 00:00:19.945
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.168
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:26.041
Skim.

7
00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:29.839
Skim means to read quickly for the general idea.

8
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.055
Skim the text first.

9
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.163
Your turn. Say: Skim.

10
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:38.815
Skim.

11
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.319
Scan.

12
00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:43.757
Scan means to look quickly for one detail.

13
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:45.839
Scan for the date.

14
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.882
Your turn. Say: Scan.

15
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:52.607
Scan.

16
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.061
Heading.

17
00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:57.096
Heading means the title of a section.

18
00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:58.893
Read each heading.

19
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:01.938
Your turn. Say: Heading.

20
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:05.546
Heading.

21
00:01:06.283 --> 00:01:07.029
Keyword.

22
00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:09.854
Keyword means an important word.

23
00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:11.869
Underline the keyword.

24
00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:15.054
Your turn. Say: Keyword.

25
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:18.785
Keyword.

26
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:20.586
Overview.

27
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:23.687
Overview means a short general view.

28
00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:25.760
Get an overview first.

29
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:28.724
Your turn. Say: Overview.

30
00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:32.533
Overview.

31
00:01:33.283 --> 00:01:34.284
Locate.

32
00:01:35.283 --> 00:01:36.865
Locate means to find.

33
00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.055
Locate the answer fast.

34
00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:42.360
Your turn. Say: Locate.

35
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.329
Locate.

36
00:01:47.083 --> 00:01:47.783
Predict.

37
00:01:48.783 --> 00:01:51.096
Predict means to guess what comes next.

38
00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:52.963
Predict the topic.

39
00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.912
Your turn. Say: Predict.

40
00:01:58.767 --> 00:01:59.396
Predict.

41
00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:01.116
Purpose.

42
00:02:02.117 --> 00:02:04.128
Purpose means the reason for writing.

43
00:02:04.717 --> 00:02:06.298
Find the writer's purpose.

44
00:02:06.883 --> 00:02:09.594
Your turn. Say: Purpose.

45
00:02:12.433 --> 00:02:13.295
Purpose.

46
00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:17.588
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:21.587
Visal, how do I read a long text in an exam?

48
00:02:22.683 --> 00:02:31.884
First skim: read the title, headings and the first line of each paragraph to get the main idea. This takes less than a minute.

49
00:02:32.983 --> 00:02:34.426
And for the questions?

50
00:02:35.517 --> 00:02:45.054
Underline the keywords in each question, then scan the text for the same word or a synonym. Read carefully only around that place.

51
00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.848
Should I read every word?

52
00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:58.176
Not at first. Skim, scan and then read closely only where you need to. This saves time and improves accuracy.

53
00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:00.834
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.683 --> 00:03:05.146
Grammar focus: Imperatives for study instructions.

55
00:03:05.446 --> 00:03:06.644
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:09.036
Skim the headings first.

57
00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.648
Scan the text for the date.

58
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:18.886
Use the base verb for instructions, such as Skim the text or Underline the keyword. Add do not for a warning.

59
00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.220
Be careful! Don't say: Skimming means read every word.

60
00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.956
Say: Skimming means reading for the main idea.

61
00:03:28.256 --> 00:03:29.965
Use -ing after means.

62
00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:33.396
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.491
A Reading Test.

64
00:03:35.791 --> 00:03:38.453
Vuthy has twenty minutes to read a long article.

65
00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.745
He skims the title and headings first.

66
00:03:42.733 --> 00:03:45.383
Then he underlines the keywords in each question.

67
00:03:46.367 --> 00:03:49.353
He scans the text for each keyword or its synonym.

68
00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:53.272
He finishes with five minutes to check his answers.

69
00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:58.194
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:01.665
To skim is to read for the blank idea.

71
00:04:01.965 --> 00:04:05.491
A, main. B, smallest. C, last.

72
00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:10.557
The answer is A: main.

73
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.728
To scan is to look for one blank.

74
00:04:14.028 --> 00:04:17.461
A, song. B, detail. C, joke.

75
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.116
The answer is B: detail.

76
00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:25.994
You skim the headings blank.

77
00:04:26.294 --> 00:04:29.704
A, never. B, last. C, first.

78
00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:35.127
The answer is C: first.

79
00:04:36.283 --> 00:04:38.097
A keyword is an blank word.

80
00:04:38.397 --> 00:04:42.167
A, important. B, empty. C, silent.

81
00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.059
The answer is A: important.

82
00:04:49.217 --> 00:04:51.344
How much time did Vuthy have left?

83
00:04:51.644 --> 00:04:55.889
A, an hour. B, five minutes. C, none.

84
00:04:59.433 --> 00:05:02.129
The answer is B: five minutes.

85
00:05:03.333 --> 00:05:06.357
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:07.217 --> 00:05:09.297
How do you read a long text quickly?

87
00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:19.584
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:19.884 --> 00:05:30.863
First I skim the title and headings to get the main idea. Then I underline the keywords in the questions and scan the text for them. I read closely only around the answer.

89
00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:32.733
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:33.617 --> 00:05:38.533
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and imperatives for study instructions.

91
00:05:38.833 --> 00:05:43.006
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

92
00:05:43.306 --> 00:05:45.854
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

93
00:05:46.154 --> 00:05:49.294
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

